From 5792dafbda396e057738309fd541d5f717fd6a2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HFM <hfm@example.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 13:21:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] subsys/pmci/mctp: add MCTP-over-SMBus/I2C binding (DSP0237
 v1.2)

Add the standard DMTF DSP0237 MCTP-over-SMBus/I2C transport binding, wire
compatible with the Linux kernel mctp-i2c driver used by OpenBMC.

Packets are carried as SMBus block writes (command code 0x0F, byte count,
source address, MCTP packet, trailing SMBus PEC). The guest is the bus
controller for TX (i2c_write) and registers as an I2C target for RX; the
target callbacks reassemble a block write and a single decode entry point
(mctp_i2c_input) validates the command code, byte count and PEC before
handing the packet to the MCTP core.

An optional link_write hook lets the framed wire buffer be routed without a
real controller, which the new pldm/i2c_loopback sample uses to round-trip
PLDM Type 0 through the full DSP0237 framing/PEC path. Verified on
qemu_riscv32.
